        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8ccecaae-a0d5-510c-99ce-b0290047f0da",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Saipan, Battle of Manila (1945)\n- Places: Saipan, Mariana Islands, Manila, Philippines\n- Military units: U.S. 2nd Marine Division, 4th Marine Division, 27th Infantry Division, Imperial Japanese Army 43rd Infantry Division\n- People: Holland Smith, Yoshitsugu Saito\n- Structures: Japanese 20mm Cannon Blockhouse\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Saipan was fought on the island of Saipan in the Mariana Islands from 15 June to 9 July 1944 as part of the Pacific campaign of World War II.\n- In 1944, Japanese forces defending Saipan hastily built the Japanese 20mm Cannon Blockhouse.\n- Early in the Battle of Saipan, Allied forces captured the Japanese 20mm Cannon Blockhouse.\n- In the Battle of Saipan, the U.S. 2nd Marine Division, 4th Marine Division, and 27th Infantry Division under Lieutenant General Holland Smith defeated the Imperial Japanese Army 43rd Infantry Division under Lieutenant General Yoshitsugu Saito.\n- The Battle of Manila (1945) was fought in Manila, the capital of the Philippines, by American and Filipino forces against Japanese troops.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6d5c618a-a404-5093-bdcd-e8a941e0be8c",
        "text": "Page: Battle of Saipan. Sentence: The Battle of Saipan was a battle of the Pacific campaign of World War II, fought on the island of Saipan in the Mariana Islands from 15 June to 9 July 1944.\nPage: Battle of Saipan. Sentence: The U.S. 2nd Marine Division, 4th Marine Division, and the Army's 27th Infantry Division, commanded by Lieutenant General Holland Smith, defeated the 43rd Infantry Division of the Imperial Japanese Army, commanded by Lieutenant General Yoshitsugu Saito.\nPage: Battle of Manila (1945). Sentence: It was fought by American and Filipino forces against Japanese troops in Manila, the capital city of the Philippines.\nPage: Japanese 20mm Cannon Blockhouse. Sentence: It was built in some haste by the Japanese forces defending Saipan in 1944, and was captured by Allied forces early in the Battle of Saipan.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
